# breezy-desktop Nix package

Unofficial Nix packaging of [Breezy Desktop](https://github.com/wheaney/breezy-desktop)
(XR glasses driver + GNOME extension + settings UI) for NixOS.

Upstream issue tracking Nix packaging: https://github.com/wheaney/breezy-desktop/issues/121

## Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `default.nix` | Top-level package — pins version, fetches source, wires subpackages |
| `xrlinuxdriver.nix` | `xrDriver` daemon, `xr_driver_cli`, `xr_driver_verify`, udev rules, systemd unit |
| `breezy-gnome.nix` | GNOME shell extension + `breezydesktop` settings UI + `virtualdisplay` binary |
| `*.patch` | Fixes for upstream bugs (see patch comments in `xrlinuxdriver.nix`) |

## Usage

As a nixpkgs overlay (e.g. from this directory):

```nix
nixpkgs.overlays = [
  (final: prev: {
    breezy-desktop = final.callPackage ./breezy { };
  })
];
```

Then `pkgs.breezy-desktop` is a `symlinkJoin` of both subpackages. The GNOME
extension UUID is exposed at `pkgs.breezy-desktop.extensionUuid` for use with
`services.gnome.gnome-shell.extensions` or similar.

## What gets installed

- `bin/xrDriver` — background daemon that owns the USB device
- `bin/xr_driver_cli` — CLI to read/write driver config
- `bin/xr_driver_verify` — licence/feature verification helper
- `bin/breezydesktop` — GTK4 settings application
- `bin/virtualdisplay` — virtual display utility
- `share/gnome-shell/extensions/breezydesktop@xronlinux.com/` — GNOME extension
- `lib/udev/rules.d/` — udev rules for XR device access
- `lib/systemd/user/xr-driver.service` — upstream systemd unit (paths rewritten)

## Platform support

`x86_64-linux` and `aarch64-linux`. Upstream bundles prebuilt shared libraries
(SteamVR overlay, etc.) for both architectures; `autoPatchelfHook` patches their
ELF interpreter/rpath so they work under NixOS.

## Updating

Change `version` and `sha256` in `default.nix`. The Cargo lock path is derived
from `source.src`, so `cargoDeps` in `xrlinuxdriver.nix` updates automatically.
Check whether any of the patches still apply cleanly after an upstream bump.

## Known NixOS integration requirements

The upstream systemd unit and udev rules are included in the derivation output
but are **not** wired up automatically — you need to install them via your
NixOS configuration. A full integration also needs:

- `~/.local/bin/xr_driver_cli` symlink (the GNOME extension's keyboard toggle
  looks for the CLI at `$XDG_BIN_HOME/xr_driver_cli` then `/usr/bin/xr_driver_cli`)
- `fs.protected_regular=1` workaround: `/dev/shm` state files are created by
  `xrDriver`; if another user's stale files exist, `fopen(..., O_CREAT)` fails
  silently (fixed by `state-null-check.patch`) but the files still need cleaning
  before restart

## Extension debugging

Logs: `~/.local/state/breezy_gnome/logs/gjs/YYYY-MM-DD.log` (not the journal).

Enable verbose output:
```bash
gsettings set com.xronlinux.BreezyDesktop debug true
```

"Ready, enabling XR effect" = effect activated successfully.
"device stream not being received" = `breezy_desktop_running` stayed false,
meaning the driver didn't signal readiness (check `xrDriver` logs / licence fetch).
